{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}]},{"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Core Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Importing at call sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"anchor":"Comparison","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Comparison"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}]},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registration-Order","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Registration Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"service-result action","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state slice","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}]},{"anchor":"Next-Steps","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Next Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"title":"Explanation","generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","title":"Architecture & Performance","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"title":"Undo \/ Redo","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","title":"EntityStore","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","title":"Security Posture","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","title":"PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","type":"topic","title":"Design Principles"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Store","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}]}}}